index 0000000..d694edd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/deployment.md
@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@
+# Deploying Fizzy on one box
+
+Fizzy can run on a single Linux server with Docker. The web server, background
+jobs, SQLite databases, cache, Action Cable, and uploaded files all live in one
+container. Kamal's proxy terminates SSL, and a named Docker volume keeps
+everything under `/rails/storage` across deploys.
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+- A Linux server with Docker installed and ports 80 and 443 open.
+- SSH access to that server. Kamal defaults to the `root` user; if you use a
+  different user, add it under `ssh` in `config/deploy.yml`.
+- A DNS record for your Fizzy hostname pointing at the server.
+- A container registry account where you can push an image. The default
+  configuration uses GitHub Container Registry (GHCR); create a personal
+  access token with `write:packages` permission and use your GitHub username
+  in the image and registry settings.
+- An SMTP account for magic-link sign-in emails and notifications.
+
+## Configure the deployment
+
+Edit `config/deploy.yml` and replace:
+
+- `image` and `registry.username` with your registry repository and username.
+  With the default GHCR configuration, use `<github-user>/fizzy` as the image
+  (Kamal prepends `ghcr.io` from `registry.server`).
+- `servers.web` with the IP address or DNS name of your server.
+- `proxy.host` and `APP_HOST` with the same public hostname.
+- `SMTP_ADDRESS`, `SMTP_PORT`, `SMTP_USERNAME`, and `MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS` with
+  your mail provider's details.
+- `builder.arch` if the server is not amd64.
+
+The mail settings are injected as environment variables and consumed by
+`config/environments/production.rb`. `SMTP_PASSWORD` is a secret and is not
+stored in `config/deploy.yml`.
+
+## Set secrets
+
+`.kamal/secrets` contains no credentials. It reads the following variables from
+your environment whenever you run a Kamal command:
+
+```sh
+export SECRET_KEY_BASE="$(bin/rails secret)"
+export KAMAL_REGISTRY_PASSWORD="<token with permission to push packages>"
+export SMTP_PASSWORD="<your SMTP password>"
+
+# Optional: only needed if you use Rails encrypted credentials.
+# export RAILS_MASTER_KEY="$(cat config/master.key)"
+```
+
+For GHCR, create a personal access token with `write:packages` permission and
+use your GitHub username as the registry username in `config/deploy.yml`. You
+can source these exports from a private file or password manager rather than
+typing them for every command. Never commit the values.
+
+## First deploy
+
+Once DNS resolves to the server and the secrets are exported, run:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal setup
+```
+
+Kamal will install Docker if needed, build and push the image, start the
+container behind kamal-proxy, obtain a Let's Encrypt certificate, and run
+`db:prepare` through the Docker entrypoint. Fizzy should then be available at
+`https://your-hostname`.
+
+Sign up with the email address you want to use as the first account owner. The
+magic-link email is delivered through the SMTP settings you configured.
+
+## Subsequent deploys
+
+Export the same secrets and run:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal deploy
+```
+
+The `fizzy_storage:/rails/storage` volume survives container replacement. It
+contains all SQLite databases, including the Solid Queue, cache, and Action
+Cable databases, plus Active Storage files. Do not remove the volume when
+updating Fizzy.
+
+Solid Queue runs inside the Puma process (`SOLID_QUEUE_IN_PUMA: true`), so
+background jobs run on the same box without a separate job server or container.
+
+Useful commands:
+
+```sh
+bin/kamal logs
+bin/kamal console
+bin/kamal shell
+```
